  "details": "I recently upgraded my PC with a new CPU and Motherboard and ever since that upgrade whenever I play VRChat player audio disappear. I will be online on PCVR or just Desktop mode for 5-10 minutes and then I get what appears like a second-long lag spike where everyone sounds robotic and their mics cut out rapidly, then poof. After just a second of that it goes quiet. No matter how many times I restart my game it keeps happening. I've tried different worlds and different groups of people and it keeps happening.\n\nKeep in mind, it's only specifically player audio. I can still hear the menu, world, music and avatar sounds.\n\nMy new CPU is a AMD Ryzen 5500 Series and the motherboard is a ROG STRYX 8550-F GAMING WIFI-II.",
